esh governor from a generic template, following the precedent this build establishes", :adr/deepened-to-implemented "cloud-itonami-isic-4711", :adr/no-still-blueprint-swap-needed-4711 "kotoba-lang/industry's own test/kotoba/industry_test.clj currently references \"9101\" (set during ictrepair/9511's own promotion) as its still-blueprint example -- \"4711\" was not the referenced example, so no swap was needed this time", :adr/already-published-decision-rule "unlike every prior sibling, this blueprint's own docs/business-model.md already published a fully detailed :retail-governor Decision Rule (approve/reject conditions, a required-technologies table, a companion playable prototype tie-in to network-isekai's 'ITONAMI: Retail Shift', ADR-2607031000) BEFORE this actor's code existed. This build implements that published design faithfully rather than inventing an architecture from a generic template", :adr/blueprint-field-sync-fix-4711 "unlike the last several builds, this repo's blueprint.edn DID need a field-sync fix: :required-technologies was missing :robotics (present in the kotoba-lang/industry registry's own entry for \"4711\" but absent from the blueprint's own list) -- fixed as part of this promotion", :adr/distinctive-checks-4711 "TWO genuinely new checks: (1) ean13-invalid-violations -- delegates to kotoba.retail/ean13-valid? rather than reimplementing the GS1 checksum, a genuinely NEW SUB-CATEGORY in the unconditional-evaluation discipline (reusing a CAPABILITY LIBRARY's own validated function rather than a sibling actor's check), the 71st distinct application overall (most recently ictrepair.governor/media-sanitization-unconfirmed-violations at 70th); (2) price-band-violation-violations -- the FLAGSHIP genuinely new check, grep-verified absent fleet-wide, the 72nd distinct application, grounded in real unit-pricing/price-marking law: the US NIST Handbook 130 (adopted by most states), the UK's Price Marking Order 2004, Germany's Preisangabenverordnung (PAng